# Contract Intelligence Platform — agent rules

Read [docs/PRODUCT_SPEC.md](../docs/PRODUCT_SPEC.md), [docs/CURRENT_STATE_AUDIT.md](../docs/CURRENT_STATE_AUDIT.md), and [docs/WORK_TRAIL.md](../docs/WORK_TRAIL.md) before implementing features. After any session that ships, blocks, or changes direction, update `docs/WORK_TRAIL.md` (session log + next work). Do not leave platform status only in chat.

## Product phases

- **Canonical product phases 1–9** govern product maturity ([BUILD_PLAN.md](../docs/BUILD_PLAN.md)).
- **Legacy engineering IDs 0–14** stay on migrations and `PHASE*_ACCEPTANCE.md` — do not rename.
- **Legacy Phase 2 (RLS/tenancy) is Foundation (canonical Phase 1), not the Historical Pilot.**
- **Canonical Phase 2 = Historical Pilot** (20–30 complete L&P packages). It has **not started** (0 packages).
- Passing a legacy acceptance script does **not** mean the corresponding product phase is complete.

## What not to build

- Not a CRM: no leads, contact cadence, sales activities, client-facing auth, client portal, or customer self-service.
- `clients` = buyer/agency procurement intelligence, not CRM accounts.
- Do not fabricate procurement intelligence, analytics, or reports without verified evidence.
- Do not claim a feature is complete because a route or table exists.

## Early UX — KEEP + FREEZE

Intelligence screens (Ask, Market, Reports, Win/Loss, Content) exist ahead of the verified corpus. **Do not expand** until Historical Pilot validates the model. Do not delete them.

## Architecture lock

Preserve: Supabase Storage vault, Vercel Workflow lifecycle, JobPort, Supabase Cron, PDF.js, openpyxl, AI Gateway abstraction, pgvector in Postgres. Do not revert to Drive-only vault, Queues-as-lifecycle, Pinecone, or LangGraph-for-ingest.

